WEBVTT

0
00:00:01.000 --> 00:00:04.000
Downloaded From www.AllSubs.org

1
00:03:52.899 --> 00:03:54.662
<i>- Fuck!
- It's not there.</i>

2
00:03:54.768 --> 00:03:56.963
It's in the kitchen where you left it.

3
00:03:57.070 --> 00:03:58.935
How'd you get in?

4
00:04:01.708 --> 00:04:03.676
You have a nice family.

5
00:04:06.146 --> 00:04:08.706
They're fine. Alive.

6
00:04:08.815 --> 00:04:11.147
Asleep.

7
00:04:13.320 --> 00:04:15.481
- Are you gonna kill me?
- If I was gonna kill you...

8
00:04:15.588 --> 00:04:17.988
I'd have done it when you walked
to the car this morning...

9
00:04:18.091 --> 00:04:21.060
<i>been gone by the time
your body hit the sidewalk.</i>

10
00:04:21.161 --> 00:04:25.063
- Then why are you here?
- To talk.

11
00:04:25.165 --> 00:04:28.464
But, Mike, if you make me kill you,
you will not go alone.

12
00:04:28.568 --> 00:04:30.968
Sit.

13
00:04:43.416 --> 00:04:45.316
Are you a good man, Inspector?

14
00:04:46.920 --> 00:04:49.582
- I think.
- And yet you've killed men.

15
00:04:51.591 --> 00:04:54.253
- Yes.
- I'm gonna ask you a question.

16
00:04:54.361 --> 00:04:58.320
How you answer it
will determine how this night ends.

17
00:04:58.431 --> 00:05:02.731
How does a good man
decide when to kill?

18
00:05:04.270 --> 00:05:07.671
<i>The man you've been chasing
is a killer, a ghost.</i>

19
00:05:10.777 --> 00:05:15.714
<i>Rumor has it that he works for a group
known only as "the organization."</i>

20
00:05:15.815 --> 00:05:18.010
<i>So secret, no one knows it exists.</i>

21
00:05:18.118 --> 00:05:22.020
<i>It takes no sides,
yet it has ties to every government.</i>

22
00:05:23.556 --> 00:05:26.184
<i>Its sole purpose is
the training and conditioning...</i>

23
00:05:26.292 --> 00:05:28.192
<i>of professional killers.</i>

24
00:05:29.295 --> 00:05:32.287
<i>These men are selected at birth...</i>

25
00:05:32.399 --> 00:05:34.560
<i>rejects, orphans...</i>

26
00:05:34.667 --> 00:05:38.125
<i>all of them unwanted and disposable.</i>

27
00:05:38.238 --> 00:05:41.639
<i>They are made experts
in every aspect of combat...</i>

28
00:05:41.640 --> 00:05:43.280
<i>and programmed for one purpose:</i>

29
00:05:44.177 --> 00:05:46.737
<i>to kill.</i>

30
00:05:46.846 --> 00:05:50.646
<i>The man you have been chasing
for the last three years, Inspector...</i>

31
00:05:50.750 --> 00:05:53.378
<i>is the very best of them.</i>

32
00:05:53.486 --> 00:05:55.386
<i>Put him there.</i>

33
00:06:05.098 --> 00:06:08.124
You shouldn't have
stolen from me, Brother.

34
00:06:08.234 --> 00:06:09.929
Now you must pay.

35
00:06:20.647 --> 00:06:22.706
Why you do that kind of thing?

36
00:06:24.717 --> 00:06:26.048
Still waiting.

37
00:06:26.152 --> 00:06:28.620
I'm sorry.

38
00:06:28.721 --> 00:06:30.621
What happened to his voice?

39
00:06:30.723 --> 00:06:32.714
He made me swallow.

40
00:06:32.826 --> 00:06:35.124
What did you do to his voice?

41
00:06:35.228 --> 00:06:39.324
Nothing, Ovie.
Exactly as he was delivered.

42
00:06:39.432 --> 00:06:41.662
Delivered?

43
00:06:41.768 --> 00:06:44.259
You didn't find him?

44
00:06:44.370 --> 00:06:46.895
No. A contractor.
An American.

45
00:06:50.009 --> 00:06:52.136
Swallow what?

46
00:06:55.381 --> 00:06:57.747
- Swallow what?
- A bomb.

47
00:06:57.851 --> 00:07:00.843
A bomb. A bomb.

48
00:07:00.954 --> 00:07:03.081
Run!

49
00:07:11.164 --> 00:07:14.133
<i>We have all heard your theories, Inspector.</i>

50
00:07:14.234 --> 00:07:16.532
This isn't a theory.

51
00:07:16.636 --> 00:07:20.663
<i>This is our guy;
no motive, no forensic evidence, no witnesses.</i>

52
00:07:20.773 --> 00:07:22.798
He's a... He's a ghost.

53
00:07:22.909 --> 00:07:26.174
And how long have you been
chasing this "ghost"?

54
00:07:26.279 --> 00:07:28.179
Three years.

55
00:07:28.281 --> 00:07:31.648
Well, thank goodness you have Interpol
to finance your persistence, huh?

56
00:07:31.751 --> 00:07:34.652
<i>You see, Inspector,
despite being the anus of the third world...</i>

57
00:07:34.754 --> 00:07:37.279
we attempt to have
competent police work here.

58
00:07:37.390 --> 00:07:40.450
And it is our belief that Bwana Ovie
was killed by his own brother.

59
00:07:40.560 --> 00:07:42.960
<i>Oh, so he choked down
a pound of C-4...</i>

60
00:07:43.062 --> 00:07:45.394
and knocked on Ovie's door?

61
00:07:45.498 --> 00:07:48.058
Probably.

62
00:07:48.168 --> 00:07:52.571
<i>General, this man truly is
the best at what he does.</i>

63
00:07:52.672 --> 00:07:56.472
He is likely responsible
for over 100 deaths.

64
00:07:56.576 --> 00:07:58.737
<i>Let me show you what I mean.</i>

65
00:08:00.113 --> 00:08:02.843
This is Ovie.

66
00:08:07.654 --> 00:08:10.452
<i>And these are just
the ones we know about.</i>

67
00:08:11.558 --> 00:08:13.992
<i>Are you beginning
to get the picture?</i>

68
00:08:36.482 --> 00:08:39.246
They might kill you for that.

69
00:08:40.954 --> 00:08:44.390
For what you're doing to that whiskey;
brutalizing it with ice.

70
00:08:47.393 --> 00:08:50.385
But never more than two cubes.
It waters down the scotch.

71
00:08:52.532 --> 00:08:54.432
- Oh.
- l... I'm sorry.

72
00:08:54.534 --> 00:08:58.265
Aftermath of my pretentious
ex-husband, I'm afraid.

73
00:08:58.371 --> 00:09:00.635
No.

74
00:09:02.342 --> 00:09:04.902
I'm June. And you are?

75
00:09:08.014 --> 00:09:10.482
This is where you tell me your name.

76
00:09:11.818 --> 00:09:14.013
Excuse me.

77
00:11:05.031 --> 00:11:07.124
Africa job complete.

78
00:11:07.233 --> 00:11:10.168
The money has been wired
to your account.

79
00:11:10.269 --> 00:11:13.898
<i>Nice work. Regrettably,
the next target date...</i>

80
00:11:14.006 --> 00:11:16.941
has been moved up
at the client's request.

81
00:11:17.043 --> 00:11:20.877
And the client wishes it
to be public.

82
00:11:20.980 --> 00:11:24.575
I've planned
something more... subtle.

83
00:11:24.684 --> 00:11:26.675
I've made preparations.

84
00:11:26.786 --> 00:11:29.778
Incumbent Russian president
Mikhail Belicoff's...

85
00:11:29.889 --> 00:11:32.790
recent political shift
is in direct conflict...

86
00:11:32.892 --> 00:11:37.693
with our client's interests and threatens
their control of the Russian government.

87
00:11:37.797 --> 00:11:39.731
The client needs it to be public.

88
00:11:39.832 --> 00:11:42.733
Do you accept the new parameters?

89
00:11:45.138 --> 00:11:48.972
- Yes.
- We appreciate you breaking your normal protocol.

90
00:11:49.075 --> 00:11:51.703
The specifics are being uploaded.

91
00:12:07.193 --> 00:12:09.491
I, for one, will not let
their cowardice deter me.

92
00:12:25.545 --> 00:12:29.948
<i>Belicoff! Belicoff! Belicoff!</i>

93
00:12:58.811 --> 00:13:02.508
Mr. Belicoff? I'm sorry.
In light of your political positions...

94
00:13:02.615 --> 00:13:05.209
do you think the hard-liners
will continue to support your reelection?

95
00:13:05.318 --> 00:13:07.218
One only needs to look at...

96
00:13:58.371 --> 00:14:02.102
We have a problem.
There was a witness in Saint Petersburg.

97
00:14:02.208 --> 00:14:04.733
How reliable are your sources?

98
00:14:04.844 --> 00:14:07.039
Impeccable, as always.

99
00:14:07.146 --> 00:14:09.637
<i>Interpol has arranged a pickup.</i>

100
00:14:09.749 --> 00:14:12.912
<i>- Will you intercept?
- Yes.</i>

101
00:14:13.019 --> 00:14:15.351
Uploading data.

102
00:14:28.099 --> 00:14:29.900
[Russian] How much?

103
00:14:32.970 --> 00:14:34.550
[Russian] Bitch!

104
00:15:23.723 --> 00:15:25.918
I can't be sure.

105
00:15:26.025 --> 00:15:28.323
He never works again so quickly.

106
00:15:28.427 --> 00:15:31.157
But the Russians say that Belicoff
was grazed by a single bullet...

107
00:15:31.263 --> 00:15:33.390
from over four kilometers away.

108
00:15:33.499 --> 00:15:36.434
But it definitely sounds like him.

109
00:15:36.535 --> 00:15:38.435
Yes, sir.

110
00:15:38.537 --> 00:15:41.802
Well, what bothers me
is that he missed.

111
00:15:41.907 --> 00:15:44.967
Yes, sir.
I know what this investigation has cost.

112
00:15:45.077 --> 00:15:47.807
 I... I understand.

113
00:15:47.913 --> 00:15:50.507
- I just need a little more time.
- Sir, you need to see this.

114
00:15:50.616 --> 00:15:52.516
Sorry, sir.
I'm gonna have to call you back.

115
00:15:55.588 --> 00:15:57.283
Okay.

116
00:15:57.390 --> 00:16:00.359
<i>- He shoots the bodyguard
to get a clean shot at Belicoff.</i>

117
00:16:00.459 --> 00:16:04.088
Yeah. He splits these two civilians
by a couple of inches. Keep watching.

118
00:16:04.196 --> 00:16:06.562
<i>Keep an eye on the bodyguard.
See that?</i>

119
00:16:06.666 --> 00:16:08.793
Back it up.
Back it up again.

120
00:16:10.436 --> 00:16:12.904
That's an awful lot
of arterial spray for a miss.

121
00:16:13.005 --> 00:16:15.030
Sir, you have call.

122
00:16:15.141 --> 00:16:17.837
<i>- This is Whittier.
- Sir, they found Belicoff's shooter.</i>

123
00:16:17.943 --> 00:16:20.969
<i>- They found him?
- Yes. Tip from a hotel concierge.</i>

124
00:16:21.080 --> 00:16:23.310
- Concierge, where?
- Grand Hotel.

125
00:16:23.416 --> 00:16:26.908
- They recognized him from a picture.
- A picture?

126
00:16:27.019 --> 00:16:29.419
- Where the hell did they get a picture?
- I don't know, sir.

127
00:16:29.522 --> 00:16:32.548
All right.
I'm on my way.

128
00:16:34.126 --> 00:16:36.026
They found him.

129
00:16:36.128 --> 00:16:38.619
Contact the Russian Secret Police
in Saint Petersburg...

130
00:16:38.731 --> 00:16:40.892
and tell them Interpol has jurisdiction.

131
00:16:41.000 --> 00:16:45.266
They're to keep him under surveillance only.
No one moves until we get there. No one!

132
00:16:52.445 --> 00:16:54.436
<i>Was the target not at the location?</i>

133
00:16:54.547 --> 00:16:58.711
<i>The girl was there, but she was no witness.
She'd never seen me before.</i>

134
00:16:58.818 --> 00:17:01.548
We will be unable to transmit payment...

135
00:17:01.654 --> 00:17:04.452
<i>for the Belicoff assignment
as the task was not completed.</i>

136
00:17:04.557 --> 00:17:08.584
<i>No. He took a direct hit through the nasal cavity.
I watched it myself.</i>

137
00:17:08.694 --> 00:17:11.026
Please wait.

138
00:17:11.130 --> 00:17:14.395
<i>Uploading live news feed.</i>

139
00:17:14.500 --> 00:17:17.401
<i>The West, so afraid of my message...</i>

140
00:17:17.503 --> 00:17:19.767
that cowardly violence
is their only response.

141
00:17:19.872 --> 00:17:22.966
<i>- And that was the scene
outside of Saint Petersburg.</i>

142
00:17:23.075 --> 00:17:26.636
Who was the client?

143
00:17:26.746 --> 00:17:28.475
Answer me!

144
00:17:29.648 --> 00:17:32.048
Who ordered the hit on Belicoff?

145
00:17:34.186 --> 00:17:37.952
If you set me up, I will find you...

146
00:17:38.057 --> 00:17:40.753
and I will burn that building
to the ground around you.

147
00:18:00.946 --> 00:18:02.846
Mike Whittier, Interpol.

148
00:18:02.948 --> 00:18:04.882
What's the status of my suspect?

149
00:18:04.984 --> 00:18:06.918
I was told you were coming, Inspector.

150
00:18:07.019 --> 00:18:10.511
I am Captain Gudnayev,
Saint Petersburg Militsiya.

151
00:18:10.623 --> 00:18:13.319
Please, make yourself comfortable.

152
00:18:13.425 --> 00:18:16.019
- My men are almost in position.
- In position for what?

153
00:18:16.128 --> 00:18:19.097
We have been informed that
the suspect intends to flee.

154
00:18:19.198 --> 00:18:21.962
- My orders are to seek-
- Whoa, whoa, whoa. Orders? Orders from who?

155
00:18:22.067 --> 00:18:26.003
- Interpol has jurisdiction here.
- Militsiya's only responsible for the extraction.

156
00:18:26.105 --> 00:18:30.007
Captain Gudnayev is not directing this operation,
I'm afraid, Inspector. I am.

157
00:18:30.109 --> 00:18:32.373
I'm Chief Agent Yuri Marklov
of the F.S.B.

158
00:18:32.478 --> 00:18:34.878
The F.S.B. Why the hell...

159
00:18:34.980 --> 00:18:37.073
is the Russian Secret Police
involved in this?

160
00:18:41.554 --> 00:18:44.114
- They're going in.
- I advise you to get your men out of there.

161
00:18:44.223 --> 00:18:46.214
You have no idea
who you're dealing with.

162
00:18:46.325 --> 00:18:48.657
<i>I assure you, these men are capable
of handling this situation.</i>

163
00:18:48.761 --> 00:18:51.730
Shoot on sight.

164
00:18:51.831 --> 00:18:55.528
Do not give that order!

165
00:19:13.853 --> 00:19:15.946
47, it's Diana.

166
00:19:16.055 --> 00:19:18.489
I could be retired
for contacting you directly.

167
00:19:20.960 --> 00:19:24.054
The client was Belicoff.

168
00:19:25.431 --> 00:19:27.831
Your location has been compromised.

169
00:19:49.788 --> 00:19:50.720
Come on.

170
00:21:04.229 --> 00:21:08.791
Stay here. Cover the elevator.
Call me on my cell and tell me where it stops.

171
00:21:59.985 --> 00:22:02.078
- Yeah.
- I've got five dead bodies in the lift, sir.

172
00:22:02.187 --> 00:22:04.747
None of them our boy.

173
00:22:04.857 --> 00:22:08.554
He's on the third floor, sir! He must have
opened the doors from inside the shaft!

174
00:22:13.932 --> 00:22:16.264
Freeze!

175
00:22:21.006 --> 00:22:22.735
Get down!

176
00:22:24.777 --> 00:22:27.268
Get down!

177
00:22:42.094 --> 00:22:44.119
Fuck!

178
00:22:44.229 --> 00:22:47.426
Sir?

179
00:22:47.533 --> 00:22:49.467
We had him.

180
00:23:05.384 --> 00:23:08.615
- How many men did you lose?
- Sixteen dead.

181
00:23:08.720 --> 00:23:12.281
No! No, no.
Wait, wait, wait, wait, wait! Don't touch that!

182
00:23:12.391 --> 00:23:15.519
Where'd you get your fucking license?

183
00:23:15.627 --> 00:23:17.788
I need the room, Captain.

184
00:24:19.992 --> 00:24:22.517
<i>Where does he get all this stuff?</i>

185
00:24:22.628 --> 00:24:24.721
Can you make it work?

186
00:24:27.299 --> 00:24:29.529
Probably. Why?

187
00:24:35.240 --> 00:24:38.266
I've been looking
for you, Inspector.

188
00:24:38.377 --> 00:24:41.244
I think we started off
on the wrong foot.

189
00:24:41.346 --> 00:24:44.577
Who informed you
of the whereabouts of my guy?

190
00:24:46.251 --> 00:24:49.277
I believe it's time
we had a chat, you and I.

191
00:24:49.388 --> 00:24:51.151
Jenkins.

192
00:24:51.256 --> 00:24:53.554
Yes, sir.

193
00:25:00.632 --> 00:25:03.157
This, uh, assassin...

194
00:25:03.268 --> 00:25:06.931
my associates tell me
you believe him to be freelance.

195
00:25:07.039 --> 00:25:09.507
Your associates tell you that?

196
00:25:09.608 --> 00:25:12.236
You do not believe he is connected
with Central Intelligence Agency?

197
00:25:12.344 --> 00:25:14.073
Why do you ask?

198
00:25:14.179 --> 00:25:17.148
No reason. It just seems a bit naive.

199
00:25:17.249 --> 00:25:19.274
Well, it's a theory.

200
00:25:19.384 --> 00:25:24.447
Yes, a theory.
But a theory shared by Moscow.

201
00:25:24.556 --> 00:25:29.084
In accordance with Article 1764.3
of the E.U. Charter...

202
00:25:29.194 --> 00:25:33.255
any state matters which deal
directly with intelligence...

203
00:25:33.365 --> 00:25:35.492
shall be the sole jurisdiction
of the host country.

204
00:25:35.601 --> 00:25:38.001
<i>Ah, and the light-bulb comes on.</i>

205
00:25:38.103 --> 00:25:40.003
Took me a minute.
Must be the jet lag.

206
00:25:40.105 --> 00:25:42.437
You're telling me to fuck off?

207
00:25:42.541 --> 00:25:46.136
No, no. Of course not.
You are a good man, Michael.

208
00:25:46.245 --> 00:25:48.372
One of Interpol's best.

209
00:25:48.480 --> 00:25:52.940
But leave this intelligence work
to the F.S.B.

210
00:25:57.322 --> 00:25:59.222
And Belicoff?

211
00:26:04.463 --> 00:26:06.363
I'm sorry?

212
00:26:06.465 --> 00:26:10.731
You know, there's two things
wrong with this photograph.

213
00:26:10.836 --> 00:26:12.736
One, the footage
has been tampered with.

214
00:26:12.838 --> 00:26:16.296
Someone inserted that civilian
to cover up what actually happened.

215
00:26:17.342 --> 00:26:19.572
Hmm.

216
00:26:19.678 --> 00:26:24.479
- And the second thing?
- My boy doesn't miss.

217
00:27:04.389 --> 00:27:07.119
<i>- Delivery.
- You're supposed to leave those at the desk.</i>

218
00:27:08.226 --> 00:27:11.059
<i>Mr. Belicoff sent them.</i>

219
00:27:18.870 --> 00:27:21.270
Make a sound, I'll end your life.
You understand?

220
00:27:21.373 --> 00:27:24.365
Who else is inside?

221
00:27:24.476 --> 00:27:26.774
<i>I know you;
from the street earlier today.</i>

222
00:27:26.878 --> 00:27:28.573
- You're coming with me.
- I can't!

223
00:27:28.680 --> 00:27:31.308
Okay, okay!
I'll get my coat.

224
00:27:42.461 --> 00:27:46.056
<i>- Where are you taking me?
- Somewhere safe.</i>

225
00:27:46.164 --> 00:27:47.961
- Get in.
- Fuck you! I'm not getting in there!

226
00:27:48.066 --> 00:27:50.466
Aaah! There's a dead man in there!

227
00:28:18.964 --> 00:28:21.956
Are you going to kill me?

228
00:28:28.740 --> 00:28:30.435
I'm gonna ask you some questions.

229
00:28:30.542 --> 00:28:34.876
<i>Before today on the street,
have you ever seen me?</i>

230
00:28:34.980 --> 00:28:37.380
<i>- Why were you there?
- My boyfriend.</i>

231
00:28:37.482 --> 00:28:40.849
- He told me to meet his driver on that corner.
- Belicoff?

232
00:28:42.254 --> 00:28:44.484
How, after I put
a bullet through his head...

233
00:28:44.589 --> 00:28:46.614
was he able to give
that speech this afternoon?

234
00:28:50.328 --> 00:28:53.525
Then you're of no use to me.

235
00:28:57.335 --> 00:28:59.269
D-Doubles. Doubles...

236
00:28:59.371 --> 00:29:01.498
Mikhail has doubles,
just like Saddam Hussein.

237
00:29:01.606 --> 00:29:04.871
The man I shot was not an impostor.
Belicoff is dead.

238
00:29:21.193 --> 00:29:23.093
Why'd you tattoo your face?

239
00:29:23.195 --> 00:29:26.858
Because it's the only place
I knew Belicoff wouldn't hit.

240
00:29:33.438 --> 00:29:36.168
Tell me about Udre Belicoff.

241
00:29:37.275 --> 00:29:39.175
Mikhail's brother?

242
00:29:39.277 --> 00:29:42.508
He runs slave girls, drugs, weapons.

243
00:29:42.614 --> 00:29:44.582
Both the C.I.A. and F.S.B.
want him dead.

244
00:29:44.683 --> 00:29:47.948
<i>- Mikhail's been protecting him.
- Get up.</i>

245
00:29:49.054 --> 00:29:50.885
- Get up. You're coming with me.
- I can't.

246
00:29:50.989 --> 00:29:53.355
He'll kill me if he finds out
I left the apartment.

247
00:29:53.458 --> 00:29:56.427
Belicoff hired me to kill him.
Used you to set me up.

248
00:29:56.528 --> 00:29:58.428
The dead man in the trunk
was your driver.

249
00:30:02.834 --> 00:30:05.428
He was gonna use it on you.

250
00:30:05.537 --> 00:30:07.698
You're as good as dead without me.

251
00:30:10.575 --> 00:30:13.373
Where are you going?

252
00:30:14.513 --> 00:30:16.708
I'm gonna finish the job
I was hired to do...

253
00:30:16.815 --> 00:30:19.613
<i>and find out who's behind this.</i>

254
00:30:32.364 --> 00:30:35.891
- I need to talk to you.
- I need coffee.

255
00:30:36.001 --> 00:30:38.993
Follow me.

256
00:30:39.104 --> 00:30:41.004
We have three roadblocks.

257
00:30:41.106 --> 00:30:43.768
Here, here, here.

258
00:30:43.875 --> 00:30:46.810
We completely shut down
international airport.

259
00:30:46.912 --> 00:30:50.177
All border security has been tripled.
He cannot get out of city.

260
00:30:50.282 --> 00:30:53.683
- What about the train stations?
- Temporarily closed.

261
00:30:53.785 --> 00:30:58.245
- And Saint Petersburg Station?
- There are no trains leaving Russia
from this station.

262
00:30:58.356 --> 00:31:00.347
<i>Only commuter trains
headed towards interior.</i>

263
00:31:01.860 --> 00:31:05.455
What make you think
he go further into Russia?

264
00:31:05.564 --> 00:31:07.657
<i>Because I know him
better than anyone.</i>

265
00:31:11.369 --> 00:31:13.599
Thanks for the coffee.

266
00:31:28.887 --> 00:31:30.787
Go to the last platform and wait.

267
00:31:32.857 --> 00:31:35.087
- Why?
- Now.

268
00:31:58.550 --> 00:32:01.280
- Jenkins, anything?
- Nothing.

269
00:32:01.386 --> 00:32:03.286
Stay sharp.

270
00:32:05.323 --> 00:32:08.349
<i>I don't know, sir.
It seems odd for him to come here.</i>

271
00:32:08.460 --> 00:32:10.724
Trust me. This is where he'll be.

272
00:32:47.499 --> 00:32:49.558
Jenkins; bench, shaved head.

273
00:32:51.803 --> 00:32:53.737
Got him, boss.

274
00:33:06.584 --> 00:33:08.415
Fuck!

275
00:33:11.589 --> 00:33:14.057
Jenkins?

276
00:33:22.734 --> 00:33:26.465
I'm still on him, boss. Platform...

277
00:33:26.571 --> 00:33:28.903
number nine.

278
00:33:29.007 --> 00:33:31.237
Boss?

279
00:34:51.790 --> 00:34:53.382
Gotten slow.

280
00:34:56.928 --> 00:34:58.896
Tell me why.

281
00:35:00.465 --> 00:35:02.660
Why is there a hit on me?

282
00:35:07.205 --> 00:35:08.900
Stay here.

283
00:36:31.623 --> 00:36:33.955
How about dying
with a little dignity?

284
00:39:48.286 --> 00:39:52.518
<i>You think it's done?
It's just beginning.</i>

285
00:40:05.803 --> 00:40:08.237
I told you to wait.

286
00:40:08.339 --> 00:40:11.831
I know. I'm sorry.

287
00:40:23.121 --> 00:40:26.215
<i>l... I know...</i>

288
00:40:32.230 --> 00:40:34.391
Shh.

289
00:40:44.976 --> 00:40:47.342
Aaah!

290
00:40:47.445 --> 00:40:50.505
Freeze!

291
00:40:57.121 --> 00:41:00.090
You're the one who's been tracking me.

292
00:41:01.659 --> 00:41:03.957
The Russian Militsiya have got
the terminal locked down.

293
00:41:04.061 --> 00:41:06.291
<i>If you need a hostage...</i>

294
00:41:06.397 --> 00:41:09.230
take me.

295
00:41:09.333 --> 00:41:10.891
Come on.

296
00:41:11.002 --> 00:41:14.062
He hasn't seen your face.
He doesn't have to die.

297
00:41:14.172 --> 00:41:14.934
Take me instead.

298
00:41:38.729 --> 00:41:40.822
Please.

299
00:41:40.932 --> 00:41:43.799
Stop.

300
00:41:50.107 --> 00:41:52.007
She saved your life.

301
00:42:20.304 --> 00:42:22.204
He said your ribs are broken.

302
00:42:22.306 --> 00:42:25.469
Unlucky.

303
00:42:28.446 --> 00:42:31.006
- You seem awfully calm, considering.
- Your assassin is dead.

304
00:42:33.117 --> 00:42:35.176
Why are you covering this up?

305
00:42:35.286 --> 00:42:37.379
You know that's not our killer.

306
00:42:37.488 --> 00:42:41.481
I told you before, Inspector,
this is no longer your affair.

307
00:42:41.592 --> 00:42:43.856
Now there are two ways
in which we may proceed.

308
00:42:43.961 --> 00:42:45.986
One, my men will
accompany you to the hospital...

309
00:42:46.097 --> 00:42:48.292
and, when you and your associate
are able to travel...

310
00:42:48.399 --> 00:42:50.799
they will escort you to the airport.

311
00:42:50.901 --> 00:42:54.462
Then I will write a report
extolling Interpol for its help.

312
00:42:54.572 --> 00:42:56.904
Medals will probably be involved.

313
00:42:57.008 --> 00:42:59.533
Or I can report your incompetence...

314
00:42:59.644 --> 00:43:02.306
and disregard for my nation's laws
to your superiors.

315
00:43:02.413 --> 00:43:05.541
This will undoubtedly find its way
to the state prosecutor in Moscow.

316
00:43:05.650 --> 00:43:10.349
So, how do you think
we should proceed, huh?

317
00:43:15.126 --> 00:43:17.026
How about...

318
00:43:17.128 --> 00:43:19.653
go fuck yourself.

319
00:43:39.617 --> 00:43:42.051
I was running out of oxygen in there!

320
00:43:42.153 --> 00:43:44.053
<i>- Don't be dramatic.
- Dramatic?</i>

321
00:43:44.155 --> 00:43:46.680
<i>- I got rid of the body.
- I've been there for hours!</i>

322
00:43:46.791 --> 00:43:49.487
I brought you breakfast.

323
00:44:16.654 --> 00:44:19.418
I'd thank you
if I wasn't so mad at you.

324
00:44:19.523 --> 00:44:21.991
Look at me.

325
00:44:23.694 --> 00:44:27.391
Back at the station, you interfered.

326
00:44:27.498 --> 00:44:29.466
I'm sorry.

327
00:44:29.567 --> 00:44:31.467
I can't allow that.

328
00:44:33.337 --> 00:44:35.931
- I swear I'll never...
- Stop talking.

329
00:44:38.075 --> 00:44:41.533
If you're looking
for a reason not to kill me...

330
00:44:41.645 --> 00:44:44.512
I don't really have one.

331
00:44:45.850 --> 00:44:48.614
I'm not a whore by choice.

332
00:44:48.719 --> 00:44:52.678
Belicoff owns me.
I'm his property.

333
00:44:52.790 --> 00:44:57.591
Would you like to know
how much he paid for me? 300, American.

334
00:45:00.498 --> 00:45:03.433
I've tried to escape.
The last time...

335
00:45:47.344 --> 00:45:49.574
It is a strange thing to wish to die.

336
00:45:56.053 --> 00:45:58.214
So, are you...

337
00:45:58.322 --> 00:46:00.950
going to kill me?

338
00:46:03.227 --> 00:46:05.320
No.

339
00:46:07.064 --> 00:46:09.999
You don't want to fuck me
and you don't want to kill me.

340
00:46:10.100 --> 00:46:13.126
I've never felt so much indifference
in my entire life.

341
00:46:16.907 --> 00:46:20.673
- If you ever again interfere with me like that...
- I won't.

342
00:46:22.079 --> 00:46:24.047
- Are we clear?
- Yeah.

343
00:46:26.684 --> 00:46:29.847
Eat your sandwich.
I need to get some sleep.

344
00:46:33.858 --> 00:46:35.758
- You know...
- Nika...

345
00:46:35.860 --> 00:46:39.057
- Yes?
- Stop talking or I'll put you back in the trunk.

346
00:47:04.500 --> 00:47:05.800
[Russian]

347
00:47:06.957 --> 00:47:08.409
Shit.

348
00:47:08.600 --> 00:47:10.400
[Russian] Get me a secure line.

349
00:47:10.405 --> 00:47:11.900
[Russian] Yes, sir.

350
00:47:19.155 --> 00:47:21.000
[Russian] Wait outside.

351
00:47:26.710 --> 00:47:28.075
<i>Da.</i>

352
00:47:28.080 --> 00:47:30.500
[Russian] If you're trying to make me nervous, Comrade,
it's clearly working.

353
00:47:30.700 --> 00:47:35.300
[Russian] Just keep it low profile
while we track him down.

354
00:47:35.800 --> 00:47:39.858
[Russian] Don't appear in public
and he won't be able to reach you.

355
00:47:40.000 --> 00:47:44.238
[Russian] Comrade Yuri, all of those bodies you buried
and yet a single man eludes me.

356
00:47:44.500 --> 00:47:48.530
[Russian] The operation will not be a success
until he and that whore are dead!

357
00:47:48.888 --> 00:47:55.220
[Russian] They are the only ones
who can ruin all of this!

358
00:47:55.706 --> 00:47:59.142
I gotta give it to you, sir. Pretty slick.

359
00:48:00.044 --> 00:48:02.410
Go fuck yourself.

360
00:48:02.513 --> 00:48:06.108
It was a pretty stupid idea actually.

361
00:48:06.216 --> 00:48:10.243
If we get caught, we'll be making
snow-cones in Siberia for the next 20 years.

362
00:48:10.354 --> 00:48:12.254
Yet here we sit.

363
00:48:12.356 --> 00:48:14.256
Shh!

364
00:48:14.260 --> 00:48:18.200
[Discreet Russian]

365
00:48:18.796 --> 00:48:20.263
Belicoff.

366
00:48:20.364 --> 00:48:23.663
Shit! Hide that thing.

367
00:48:33.410 --> 00:48:35.139
We came to see Chief Agent Yuri.

368
00:48:35.245 --> 00:48:37.440
- What's the problem?
- Chief Agent is very busy man.

369
00:48:37.548 --> 00:48:40.847
He asked you to go directly to the airport.
We'll escort you there immediately.

370
00:48:42.152 --> 00:48:44.382
Okay.

371
00:49:13.250 --> 00:49:15.150
It's for you.

372
00:49:18.589 --> 00:49:21.820
After all these years,
I'd think you'd trust me a little more than this.

373
00:49:21.925 --> 00:49:23.825
Tell me what you know.

374
00:49:23.927 --> 00:49:26.361
Officially, nothing.

375
00:49:26.463 --> 00:49:30.559
Unofficially, it appears
your employer has thrown you to the wolves.

376
00:49:30.668 --> 00:49:32.568
- Why?
- Apparently...

377
00:49:32.670 --> 00:49:34.661
Belicoff's softening political stance
and his refusal...

378
00:49:34.772 --> 00:49:37.570
to cooperate with the hard-liners
upset a lot of people.

379
00:49:37.675 --> 00:49:39.905
<i>They ordered the hit
and replaced him with one of their own.</i>

380
00:49:40.010 --> 00:49:43.707
Seems you and your friend here are the only ones
who know Belicoff is actually a double.

381
00:49:43.814 --> 00:49:46.408
What's the C.I.A.'s position?

382
00:49:46.517 --> 00:49:49.577
<i>The company usually likes to be
on the side of whoever wins.</i>

383
00:49:49.687 --> 00:49:51.712
<i>Take the envelope from the girl.</i>

384
00:49:55.392 --> 00:49:57.257
Ah.

385
00:49:57.361 --> 00:50:00.228
<i>Udre Belicoff,
Mikhail's younger brother.</i>

386
00:50:00.330 --> 00:50:02.696
<i>Rumor is you'd like him to disappear.</i>

387
00:50:02.800 --> 00:50:05.064
- That is the rumor.
- I'd like to help.

388
00:50:05.169 --> 00:50:07.694
How's killing Udre Belicoff
gonna help you?

389
00:50:07.805 --> 00:50:11.241
- Let me worry about that.
- Well, that might be worth something.

390
00:50:11.341 --> 00:50:14.208
- What do you want for your trouble?
- Small favor.

391
00:50:20.517 --> 00:50:23.384
<i>This is a small favor?
I don't think I can do this.</i>

392
00:50:23.487 --> 00:50:25.717
<i>- Not in your time frame.
- Keep reading.</i>

393
00:50:25.823 --> 00:50:27.290
Jesus Christ!

394
00:50:27.391 --> 00:50:29.325
Tell me this isn't
what I think it is.

395
00:50:29.426 --> 00:50:32.259
Okay. It's not what you think it is.

396
00:50:32.362 --> 00:50:36.822
But I'd expect the last thing you'd want
is for me to be arrested with that file.

397
00:50:40.404 --> 00:50:43.840
Okay. I'll try.

398
00:50:43.941 --> 00:50:46.000
<i>- Thank you.
- Yeah, you're welcome.</i>

399
00:50:45.828 --> 00:50:50.697
We know Udre's been planning something
with a German arms dealer named Price.

400
00:50:50.799 --> 00:50:53.131
<i>The two have never met.
That's your way in.</i>

401
00:50:53.235 --> 00:50:56.170
<i>Intercept Price,
and you get a shot at Udre.</i>

402
00:50:56.271 --> 00:50:58.171
<i>I'll get you his file.</i>

403
00:50:58.273 --> 00:51:00.537
<i>They're meeting
in Istanbul in two days.</i>

404
00:51:20.596 --> 00:51:23.394
Good morning.
Have you slept at all?

405
00:51:23.498 --> 00:51:24.829
Some.

406
00:51:28.003 --> 00:51:30.665
<i>You know, you could sleep in the bed.
I won't bite you.</i>

407
00:51:32.207 --> 00:51:34.107
Unless you pay me.

408
00:51:41.516 --> 00:51:43.416
It's not polite to stare.

409
00:51:59.167 --> 00:52:01.727
So, when are you
gonna tell me your name?

410
00:52:01.837 --> 00:52:04.635
- Get dressed.
- What for?

411
00:52:04.740 --> 00:52:08.733
We're going to dinner.
We need to buy you a new dress.

412
00:52:10.579 --> 00:52:14.447
<i>You know, you're really quite charming
when you aren't killing people.</i>

413
00:52:45.614 --> 00:52:48.640
- This place looks nice.
- Yeah.

414
00:52:48.750 --> 00:52:50.911
- Don't you think?
- Mm-hmm.

415
00:52:53.255 --> 00:52:55.689
Wait here.

416
00:53:40.969 --> 00:53:44.200
- How did you know I wouldn't just take off?
- I didn't. Come on.

417
00:53:44.306 --> 00:53:46.137
We have dinner reservations at 8:00.

418
00:53:53.815 --> 00:53:56.045
<i>Jenks, how do you feel?</i>

419
00:53:56.151 --> 00:53:59.678
My pride hurts worse than my arms.

420
00:53:59.788 --> 00:54:04.248
- Any word?
- The sketch is out to every
Interpol substation in Europe.

421
00:54:04.359 --> 00:54:07.055
Train stations, airports,
border crossings and...

422
00:54:08.463 --> 00:54:11.125
<i>- What's that?
- This is what I wanted to show you.</i>

423
00:54:11.233 --> 00:54:14.532
It's every appearance
Belicoff has made within the last 12 months.

424
00:54:14.636 --> 00:54:18.504
This is from the speech he made
in London on May the 7th.

425
00:54:18.607 --> 00:54:23.340
And this is from some shitty political luncheon
he had in northern Georgia.

426
00:54:23.445 --> 00:54:25.504
Someone took a photo
from a mobile phone.

427
00:54:25.614 --> 00:54:28.845
- Look at the date.
- May 7th.

428
00:54:28.950 --> 00:54:31.612
- How's that possible?
- I can't be sure...

429
00:54:31.720 --> 00:54:34.348
but unless he's figured out
how to be in two places at once...

430
00:54:34.456 --> 00:54:37.425
- Ha. He has a double.
- He's certainly paranoid enough.

431
00:54:37.526 --> 00:54:39.517
That explains the arterial spray.

432
00:54:39.628 --> 00:54:41.528
I hope he had health benefits.

433
00:54:48.403 --> 00:54:51.270
<i>When I was a little girl, I had this little squirrel...</i>

434
00:54:51.373 --> 00:54:53.534
<i>you know,
with black stripes on the back?</i>

435
00:54:53.642 --> 00:54:56.270
<i>- A chipmunk.
- Oh, yeah, that's right. A chipmunk.</i>

436
00:54:56.378 --> 00:54:58.539
<i>His name was Tishka.</i>

437
00:55:00.048 --> 00:55:02.710
<i>I'm sorry, sir,
but this is for another gentleman.</i>

438
00:55:02.818 --> 00:55:04.809
- Table 26?
- That's right.

439
00:55:07.189 --> 00:55:09.282
My mistake.

440
00:55:10.859 --> 00:55:13.828
You know what table that is?

441
00:55:13.929 --> 00:55:15.624
I saw the layout when we came in.

442
00:55:15.730 --> 00:55:18.961
- Do you remember everything you see?
- No, not everything.

443
00:55:19.067 --> 00:55:20.659
What's the soup of the day?

444
00:55:20.769 --> 00:55:25.103
Red lentil and mint with sautéed onions
and diced tomatoes.

445
00:55:25.207 --> 00:55:27.767
The woman sitting two tables behind you;
what's she wearing?

446
00:55:27.876 --> 00:55:30.436
- With the red hair and the silk dress, facing you?
- Yeah.

447
00:55:30.545 --> 00:55:33.173
That's not a woman.

448
00:55:44.793 --> 00:55:47.523
What color underwear am I wearing?

449
00:55:47.629 --> 00:55:49.597
You're not wearing any underwear.

450
00:56:02.611 --> 00:56:05.512
Come with us, sir.
Here we go. It's gonna be all right.

451
00:56:06.882 --> 00:56:08.907
Nika, ask for the check.

452
00:56:09.017 --> 00:56:11.645
- But I'm not done!
- Then hurry.

453
00:56:16.992 --> 00:56:19.483
You scratch what I said
about you being charming.

454
00:56:32.440 --> 00:56:34.533
Sorry, sir.

455
00:56:55.297 --> 00:56:57.356
<i>Sheiكe.</i>

456
00:57:14.049 --> 00:57:16.745
Mr. Price...

457
00:57:16.851 --> 00:57:19.081
thank you for the introduction
to Udre Belicoff.

458
00:57:22.357 --> 00:57:25.383
Little help, please.

459
00:57:40.075 --> 00:57:42.441
- What the fuck?
- Let's go.

460
00:57:42.544 --> 00:57:44.774
- What?
- Now.

461
00:57:52.954 --> 00:57:55.184
Well, that was lovely.

462
00:57:55.290 --> 00:57:57.986
Right up to the time
you dragged me out by my hair.

463
00:57:59.928 --> 00:58:01.953
Undress me.

464
00:58:02.063 --> 00:58:04.122
So very good at firearms.

465
00:58:04.232 --> 00:58:07.167
Not so good with
ladies' undergarments.

466
00:58:09.170 --> 00:58:11.502
Careful. I'm not wearing any panties.

467
00:58:11.606 --> 00:58:13.904
Nika, you're drunk.

468
00:58:14.009 --> 00:58:15.738
And?

469
00:58:15.844 --> 00:58:19.280
- And this is a very bad idea.
- Oh.

470
00:58:20.215 --> 00:58:23.810
- You mean this?
- Yes, that.

471
00:58:23.918 --> 00:58:26.113
How about this?

472
00:58:28.423 --> 00:58:30.323
Definitely that.

473
00:58:32.827 --> 00:58:35.022
Then...

474
00:58:35.130 --> 00:58:37.860
this must be really bad.

475
00:59:21.743 --> 00:59:23.734
Give me case.

476
00:59:23.845 --> 00:59:25.472
Mr. Price!

477
00:59:25.580 --> 00:59:27.673
<i>So, you took it upon yourself...</i>

478
00:59:27.782 --> 00:59:30.182
to change our appointment.

479
00:59:30.285 --> 00:59:33.584
- How forward of you.
- As I told your men downstairs...

480
00:59:33.688 --> 00:59:37.055
<i>I was attacked earlier tonight
by some lunatic.</i>

481
00:59:37.158 --> 00:59:40.025
- Common sense dictated...
- Common sense should have dictated...

482
00:59:40.128 --> 00:59:43.097
you not abuse my good nature.

483
00:59:43.198 --> 00:59:45.098
Sit.

484
00:59:51.873 --> 00:59:54.865
<i>I was just going over
a few of my lines...</i>

485
00:59:54.976 --> 00:59:57.240
<i>with some of your competitors.</i>

486
01:00:01.182 --> 01:00:03.548
<i>Lines.</i>

487
01:00:03.651 --> 01:00:05.744
<i>A few of my lines.</i>

488
01:00:05.854 --> 01:00:07.822
Do you get it?

489
01:00:08.690 --> 01:00:10.681
Where was I?

490
01:00:13.027 --> 01:00:14.927
He's not Price.

491
01:00:25.173 --> 01:00:27.073
<i>Da.</i>

492
01:00:29.811 --> 01:00:31.836
This is the, uh... the Kedr.

493
01:00:31.946 --> 01:00:34.847
<i>Nine-millimeter, compact.</i>

494
01:00:34.949 --> 01:00:37.577
It's, uh, less than two kilograms.

495
01:00:37.685 --> 01:00:40.552
Select fire single,
or fully automatic.

496
01:00:42.023 --> 01:00:43.957
Empty...

497
01:00:44.058 --> 01:00:47.118
<i>and safe.</i>

498
01:00:47.228 --> 01:00:50.561
<i>Or if you are looking for an assault rifle...</i>

499
01:00:50.665 --> 01:00:54.863
<i>I have the M203 with
under-barrel grenade launcher.</i>

500
01:00:54.969 --> 01:00:57.130
A lot of third-world dictators...

501
01:00:57.238 --> 01:00:59.729
got a lot of 7.62s stockpiled.

502
01:00:59.841 --> 01:01:02.776
Saves them from having to buy ammo.

503
01:01:02.877 --> 01:01:07.541
<i>Everything here is
available in bulk, of course.</i>

504
01:01:07.649 --> 01:01:09.674
Prices not negotiable.

505
01:01:12.620 --> 01:01:15.054
Any questions, Mr. Price?

506
01:01:15.156 --> 01:01:18.922
Yeah. What about the little one there?

507
01:01:20.128 --> 01:01:22.790
Here I show you.

508
01:01:22.897 --> 01:01:26.264
<i>This is a Makarov .22.</i>

509
01:01:26.367 --> 01:01:28.767
<i>- A favorite of the K.G.B.
- No. No.</i>

510
01:01:28.870 --> 01:01:32.237
Particularly effective
in the right hands.

511
01:01:32.340 --> 01:01:33.602
<i>But for a real target...</i>

512
01:01:33.708 --> 01:01:36.176
you need to find a soft spot.

513
01:01:36.277 --> 01:01:38.575
Whoa. Hold up. Hey!

514
01:01:38.680 --> 01:01:40.671
<i>Wait. This is not a Kedr.</i>

515
01:01:40.782 --> 01:01:42.943
It's a Chinese copy.

516
01:01:43.051 --> 01:01:46.077
In fact, I don't know if it's the drugs,
or if you're usually this inept...

517
01:01:46.187 --> 01:01:48.280
<i>but you've been wrong
about most of these weapons.</i>

518
01:01:48.389 --> 01:01:50.789
If the gun you're holding
is as cheap as this one...

519
01:01:50.892 --> 01:01:54.692
<i>even if you could manage to shoot her
in the eye; and I'm not saying you could...</i>

520
01:01:54.796 --> 01:01:56.855
<i>you wouldn't kill her.</i>

521
01:03:36.297 --> 01:03:40.131
- Why are you doing this to me?
- I need you to help me with your brother.

522
01:03:42.270 --> 01:03:45.433
Mikhail? Fine. Fuck him.

523
01:03:45.540 --> 01:03:48.304
I do whatever you want.

524
01:03:48.409 --> 01:03:50.343
What the fuck do you want me to do?

525
01:03:52.046 --> 01:03:54.014
<i>Just this.</i>

526
01:05:07.021 --> 01:05:10.548
<i>You know, it says here that when
the male penguin meets the female penguin...</i>

527
01:05:10.658 --> 01:05:14.025
he knows in the first 10 seconds
whether he's gonna like her or not.

528
01:05:15.797 --> 01:05:17.697
Are you listening?

529
01:05:17.799 --> 01:05:20.529
I'm listening.
I read that.

530
01:05:21.703 --> 01:05:23.830
These articles are full of shit.

531
01:05:23.938 --> 01:05:27.430
- Why do you buy these magazines?
- For the advertisements.

532
01:05:28.943 --> 01:05:31.605
What do you need
luggage like this for?

533
01:05:31.713 --> 01:05:34.739
Because that perfectly holds
my Blaser sniper rifle and .245.

534
01:05:34.849 --> 01:05:37.784
And a gag for irritating,
talkative little girls like yourself.

535
01:05:37.885 --> 01:05:39.853
You want me to stop and get it out?

536
01:05:39.954 --> 01:05:42.081
I don't know.
You think we have time for foreplay?

537
01:05:56.370 --> 01:06:01.137
You know, when I was a little girl,
my father raised grapes.

538
01:06:02.977 --> 01:06:06.071
And I told him that one day
I'd own my own vineyard.

539
01:06:14.322 --> 01:06:16.290
It looks nice.

540
01:06:22.430 --> 01:06:24.489
We need to get off the road.

541
01:06:51.459 --> 01:06:53.950
Jenks.

542
01:06:55.096 --> 01:06:57.826
Is that his suitcase?
How did we get that?

543
01:06:57.932 --> 01:07:00.730
As a consolation prize
Captain Gudnayev sent me.

544
01:07:00.835 --> 01:07:03.827
Our boy's stuff from the hotel in St. Pete
in case it might help.

545
01:07:03.938 --> 01:07:05.838
- Anything?
- Not much.

546
01:07:07.475 --> 01:07:09.773
There is this.

547
01:07:12.180 --> 01:07:14.307
What do you make of this?

548
01:07:19.253 --> 01:07:21.153
<i>"Trust unto God...</i>

549
01:07:21.255 --> 01:07:23.655
and he shall direct your path."

550
01:07:23.758 --> 01:07:25.851
- It's...
- That's Psalms.

551
01:07:25.960 --> 01:07:29.123
I never figured our boy as the religious type.

552
01:07:29.230 --> 01:07:30.822
That's strange.

553
01:07:48.816 --> 01:07:50.750
Nika.

554
01:07:50.852 --> 01:07:52.752
I have to go.

555
01:07:56.357 --> 01:07:58.689
So much for happy endings.

556
01:08:02.663 --> 01:08:04.927
I don't want you to do this.

557
01:08:06.634 --> 01:08:08.568
Belicoff needs to die.

558
01:08:10.037 --> 01:08:12.904
I don't care about that.
Not anymore.

559
01:08:13.007 --> 01:08:16.841
As long as he's alive,
they will never stop looking for you.

560
01:08:52.179 --> 01:08:54.147
Take this.

561
01:08:54.248 --> 01:08:58.309
At the next station,
get off the train as soon as it stops.

562
01:08:58.419 --> 01:09:00.546
Move with the crowd.

563
01:09:02.123 --> 01:09:04.057
But I don't even know your name.

564
01:09:04.158 --> 01:09:08.219
The place I was raised, they didn't give us names.
They gave us numbers.

565
01:09:09.330 --> 01:09:11.662
Mine was 47.

566
01:09:13.734 --> 01:09:15.964
Well, that explains a lot.

567
01:09:17.672 --> 01:09:20.334
- How will I find you?
- Don't worry.

568
01:09:20.441 --> 01:09:21.738
I'll find you.

569
01:09:22.910 --> 01:09:25.242
What are you going to do?

570
01:09:25.346 --> 01:09:27.246
What I do.

571
01:10:06.199 --> 01:10:12.105
[Russian] You have no idea of the pain
involved in the procedure.

572
01:10:13.110 --> 01:10:14.448
[Russian] They peel back the skin of the face...

573
01:10:14.500 --> 01:10:17.863
[Russian] and screw a Teflon frame to the bones
to duplicate the facial features.

574
01:10:18.030 --> 01:10:21.600
[Russian] I wonder, if I had known the pain involved...

575
01:10:21.992 --> 01:10:27.240
[Russian] would I still have gone through
with this whole double business.

576
01:10:27.500 --> 01:10:30.350
[Russian] Are you sure? Come on!

577
01:10:32.513 --> 01:10:35.482
You're drunk.

578
01:10:35.583 --> 01:10:39.314
<i>You don't want to drink
with your new president, Tovarich?</i>

579
01:10:39.420 --> 01:10:41.820
We are celebrating. Yes?

580
01:10:43.457 --> 01:10:45.254
All the evidence is erased.

581
01:10:45.359 --> 01:10:48.351
<i>Mikhail Belicoff!</i>

582
01:10:50.631 --> 01:10:53.065
And his pathetic brother Udre.

583
01:10:55.636 --> 01:10:57.536
Now I'm the one and only.

584
01:10:57.638 --> 01:11:00.300
And the one man I have
asked you to kill...

585
01:11:00.408 --> 01:11:02.569
the only one who can expose us...

586
01:11:02.676 --> 01:11:05.076
is the one man not in this room!

587
01:11:07.181 --> 01:11:09.672
So...

588
01:11:09.784 --> 01:11:11.752
tell me, Tovarich.

589
01:11:11.852 --> 01:11:14.446
What exactly
have you done to find him?

590
01:11:14.555 --> 01:11:17.422
It seems if we wait long enough...

591
01:11:17.525 --> 01:11:19.425
he will find you.

592
01:11:19.527 --> 01:11:22.360
Us, Tovarich Yuri.

593
01:11:22.463 --> 01:11:26.456
- He will find us.
- The organization has sent in their best operatives.

594
01:11:26.567 --> 01:11:30.230
<i>I know.
Don't let your incompetence hinder them.</i>

595
01:11:30.337 --> 01:11:32.532
We will not have
this conversation again.

596
01:11:50.658 --> 01:11:53.627
<i>Three hours ago, Belicoff's brother Udre
was found dead in Istanbul.</i>

597
01:11:53.727 --> 01:11:56.594
They're waiting for the body
to arrive in Moscow for the funeral.

598
01:11:56.697 --> 01:11:58.289
Heads up.

599
01:11:58.399 --> 01:12:00.833
Michael. How's things going?

600
01:12:00.935 --> 01:12:04.598
Belicoff's brother has just been found murdered.
It's him, sir. It's our guy.

601
01:12:04.705 --> 01:12:06.673
<i>He's setting Belicoff up.</i>

602
01:12:06.774 --> 01:12:10.972
We're getting pressure from the ministry
and the E.U. to drop this investigation.

603
01:12:11.078 --> 01:12:15.105
- But, sir, the Russians will...
- The Russians are the ones leading the E.U. on this.

604
01:12:15.216 --> 01:12:17.411
They blatantly deny
your ghost exists...

605
01:12:17.518 --> 01:12:19.748
and have filed papers
with the minister's office...

606
01:12:19.854 --> 01:12:21.344
claiming you've
overstepped your authority.

607
01:12:21.455 --> 01:12:23.480
Who? Who brought those allegations?

608
01:12:23.591 --> 01:12:27.459
The F.S.B.
Specifically, Chief Agent Yuri Marklov.

609
01:12:27.561 --> 01:12:29.586
I need you to stop.

610
01:12:29.697 --> 01:12:33.531
No. You don't understand.
The F.S.B. is covering this up.

611
01:12:33.634 --> 01:12:36.125
He killed Belicoff's brother.
Now why?

612
01:12:36.237 --> 01:12:38.501
<i>- Why would he do that, unless...
- Mikhail Belicoff!</i>

613
01:12:38.606 --> 01:12:41.769
announced that he would attend funeral
services tomorrow morning for the burial...

614
01:12:41.876 --> 01:12:43.867
<i>- The funeral.
- of his brother, Udre...</i>

615
01:12:43.978 --> 01:12:45.445
who died two days ago...

616
01:12:45.546 --> 01:12:47.446
He's gonna take Belicoff
at Udre's funeral.

617
01:12:47.548 --> 01:12:49.516
<i>some speculation
that Belicoff's opponent...</i>

618
01:14:16.237 --> 01:14:19.604
<i>This generator produces
over 3,000 amps...</i>

619
01:14:19.707 --> 01:14:22.369
<i>much more than is necessary, but...</i>

620
01:14:22.476 --> 01:14:25.570
I wanted you to understand
the gravity of this situation.

621
01:14:25.679 --> 01:14:28.409
<i>your hand will activate.</i>

622
01:14:28.515 --> 01:14:32.042
You'll have 30 seconds to order
the shooting of your friend Belicoff.

623
01:14:33.220 --> 01:14:36.815
If you don't,
the generator will start.

624
01:14:36.924 --> 01:14:39.916
<i>Your skin will melt.
Your blood will vaporize.</i>

625
01:14:40.027 --> 01:14:42.587
There won't be enough
left of you to identify.

626
01:14:43.697 --> 01:14:47.133
You have gone to
a great deal of trouble.

627
01:14:47.234 --> 01:14:49.065
I am just a bureaucrat.

628
01:14:49.169 --> 01:14:52.969
<i>There is nothing I can do
for you, I'm afraid.</i>

629
01:14:53.073 --> 01:14:54.062
I disagree.

630
01:14:54.174 --> 01:14:56.699
This is not a request.

631
01:14:56.810 --> 01:15:00.678
This situation is fixed,
and you know both possible outcomes.

632
01:15:00.781 --> 01:15:06.185
Live or die. Your choice.

633
01:15:06.287 --> 01:15:09.950
Here's something to keep
things in perspective.

634
01:15:12.226 --> 01:15:14.854
I picked it up last night
when I was in your house.

635
01:15:14.962 --> 01:15:16.953
You bastard!

636
01:15:17.064 --> 01:15:20.591
If I were you,
I'd keep that radio dry.

637
01:15:20.625 --> 01:15:22.100
[Russian] Asshole!

638
01:15:22.236 --> 01:15:24.830
Yell all you like.

639
01:15:24.938 --> 01:15:27.133
The Lord Himself won't hear you.

640
01:15:27.910 --> 01:15:28.999
[Russian] You asshole!

641
01:15:49.630 --> 01:15:51.621
There are over 100 highly trained...

642
01:15:51.732 --> 01:15:54.360
alpha Special Forces
soldiers in this cathedral.

643
01:15:54.468 --> 01:15:57.528
It would be foolish
to attempt any type of violence.

644
01:15:57.638 --> 01:16:00.368
A man as highly trained
as your assassin would realize this.

645
01:16:00.474 --> 01:16:03.034
What if he does?
Look around you.

646
01:16:03.143 --> 01:16:05.976
How much civilian blood
do you think will be shed?

647
01:16:06.080 --> 01:16:08.571
We are prepared for that as well.

648
01:16:08.682 --> 01:16:10.809
Gas canisters are being deployed.

649
01:16:10.918 --> 01:16:13.716
If anything should occur,
the civilians will be rendered unconscious.

650
01:16:13.821 --> 01:16:16.255
Now, if you will excuse me.

651
01:17:06.000 --> 01:17:13.519
[Addressing in Russian]

652
01:17:18.952 --> 01:17:21.580
One minute, 50 seconds.

653
01:17:30.297 --> 01:17:33.095
My brother; he was a troubled man...

654
01:17:33.200 --> 01:17:35.100
but he was not always like that.

655
01:17:36.203 --> 01:17:38.398
One minute, 25 seconds.

656
01:17:41.208 --> 01:17:43.802
<i>One minute, 20 seconds.</i>

657
01:17:43.911 --> 01:17:48.439
<i>Should we choose to be kind
and let her die much like my brother?</i>

658
01:17:48.549 --> 01:17:50.813
<i>Or should we do what is necessary...</i>

659
01:17:50.918 --> 01:17:54.046
what is hard, to save what we love?

660
01:17:55.456 --> 01:17:57.788
<i>One minute.</i>

661
01:18:01.094 --> 01:18:04.188
I, for one, will not fail again.

662
01:18:04.298 --> 01:18:07.961
Not with this country.
Not with our children's future.

663
01:18:08.068 --> 01:18:10.127
<i>Not with you, my countrymen.</i>

664
01:18:13.006 --> 01:18:14.633
<i>Thirty-five seconds.</i>

665
01:18:17.244 --> 01:18:19.474
<i>- Hurry! Come in!
- Da.</i>

666
01:18:19.580 --> 01:18:22.014
Change target.
Shoot Belicoff.

667
01:18:35.662 --> 01:18:38.859
Just fucking do it now!

668
01:18:58.819 --> 01:19:00.980
Do not let the assassin escape.

669
01:19:01.088 --> 01:19:03.022
Release the gas.

670
01:19:03.123 --> 01:19:06.786
Lock down the doors.
I suggest you and your men follow me.

671
01:19:07.728 --> 01:19:09.457
Let's go!

672
01:20:13.393 --> 01:20:15.918
Your man has made a mistake.
There is no exit.

673
01:20:16.029 --> 01:20:17.997
He's trapped.

674
01:20:21.368 --> 01:20:23.962
Doesn't make sense.

675
01:20:24.071 --> 01:20:26.733
Why would he...

676
01:20:31.945 --> 01:20:34.106
"Trust unto God...

677
01:20:36.183 --> 01:20:38.413
<i>and He shall direct your path. "</i>

678
01:20:38.518 --> 01:20:40.986
Shit. He set this up
from the very beginning.

679
01:21:35.175 --> 01:21:37.939
Where does this key fit?

680
01:21:38.045 --> 01:21:41.378
The archbishop's personal chambers.

681
01:21:41.481 --> 01:21:43.915
The third tower.
Over the Muscova.

682
01:21:45.419 --> 01:21:47.410
He's going into the river,
like in St. Pete.

683
01:21:47.521 --> 01:21:50.581
Jenks, get our men.
Let's go.

684
01:21:53.927 --> 01:21:56.487
He is in the southwest tower.
Call in the gunships.

685
01:21:56.596 --> 01:21:59.292
<i>Do not let him escape.</i>

686
01:22:00.534 --> 01:22:02.593
Seems I underestimated you.

687
01:22:03.804 --> 01:22:05.704
Consistently.

688
01:22:06.740 --> 01:22:09.038
A miscalculation on my part.

689
01:22:11.678 --> 01:22:13.509
Who are you?

690
01:22:15.982 --> 01:22:19.110
- Answer me.
- Let me help you.

691
01:22:19.219 --> 01:22:22.245
- How would you do that? By having me killed?
- Ah. No.

692
01:22:22.355 --> 01:22:24.585
For that I'm sorry.
It was a mistake.

693
01:22:24.691 --> 01:22:26.659
And Nika... was that a mistake?

694
01:22:26.760 --> 01:22:29.092
<i>- Or did you destroy her life
for your own amusement?
- What?</i>

695
01:22:29.196 --> 01:22:32.893
You think you can take
what has cost millions...

696
01:22:32.999 --> 01:22:35.900
years of planning,
for the good of this country...

697
01:22:36.002 --> 01:22:37.902
and destroy that?

698
01:22:38.004 --> 01:22:41.269
Then what? Walk away?

699
01:22:41.374 --> 01:22:45.936
You don't really think they will let you do that.
If you kill me, they will never let you go.

700
01:22:46.046 --> 01:22:48.776
They will hunt you
for the rest of your life.

701
01:22:58.358 --> 01:23:00.622
You did your job.

702
01:23:00.727 --> 01:23:03.890
And you did it very well.

703
01:23:03.997 --> 01:23:06.864
And for that, my boy,
you should be proud.

704
01:23:07.901 --> 01:23:09.801
That's it?

705
01:23:09.903 --> 01:23:13.066
Yes. I'm offering you
your life back.

706
01:23:13.173 --> 01:23:16.301
That is why you are here, yes?
That is what you want.

707
01:23:16.409 --> 01:23:18.377
Uh-uh.

708
01:23:18.478 --> 01:23:20.378
No?

709
01:23:20.480 --> 01:23:21.447
No.

710
01:24:55.475 --> 01:24:57.500
Interpol! Drop your weapons!

711
01:24:57.611 --> 01:24:59.545
<i>We have an arrest warrant for that man.</i>

712
01:25:04.517 --> 01:25:07.145
Don't move! Hands on your head!
On your head!

713
01:25:07.254 --> 01:25:09.722
- On your knees!
- Don't do anything stupid.

714
01:25:55.001 --> 01:25:57.026
Just one thing.

715
01:25:58.138 --> 01:26:01.073
Knowing how this ends,
was it worth it...

716
01:26:01.174 --> 01:26:03.233
killing Belicoff?

717
01:26:03.343 --> 01:26:05.140
Knowing how this ends?

718
01:26:05.245 --> 01:26:07.475
Definitely.

719
01:26:09.983 --> 01:26:11.883
What do you make of that?

720
01:26:14.387 --> 01:26:15.786
What the hell?

721
01:26:33.773 --> 01:26:36.264
- Who the hell are you?
- I'm Agent Smith...

722
01:26:36.376 --> 01:26:38.776
of the U.S. Central Intelligence Agency.

723
01:26:38.878 --> 01:26:42.075
- I need all you men to the rear of that vehicle.
- You don't have jurisdiction.

724
01:26:42.182 --> 01:26:44.548
We aren't here.
Which means when we open up on you...

725
01:26:44.651 --> 01:26:47.916
and shred your bodies with automatic fire,
then this will never have happened.

726
01:26:49.456 --> 01:26:50.946
- Stand down.
- We have reason to believe...

727
01:26:51.057 --> 01:26:53.116
<i>you're involved
in terrorist activities.</i>

728
01:26:53.226 --> 01:26:56.286
We're Interpol.
And in accordance with section 3...

729
01:26:56.396 --> 01:26:59.797
- We're transporting an international criminal.
- What criminal?

730
01:27:03.136 --> 01:27:05.127
You know what?
I'm sorry, man.

731
01:27:06.706 --> 01:27:08.298
My mistake.

732
01:27:08.408 --> 01:27:10.968
- I thought you were someone else.
- You prick.

733
01:27:12.679 --> 01:27:14.613
On behalf of the United States government...

734
01:27:14.714 --> 01:27:17.774
I'd like to extend to you
our sincerest apologies.

735
01:27:19.786 --> 01:27:21.310
Load up, boys.

736
01:27:50.050 --> 01:27:53.508
<i>- So now what?
- Now you have to answer my question.</i>

737
01:27:53.620 --> 01:27:56.418
Are you a good man, Inspector?

738
01:27:56.523 --> 01:27:58.923
I think.

739
01:27:59.025 --> 01:28:01.721
And yet you've killed men.

740
01:28:01.828 --> 01:28:03.227
<i>So, Inspector...</i>

741
01:28:03.329 --> 01:28:06.924
how does a good man
decide when to kill?

742
01:28:08.601 --> 01:28:11.832
If I think that a man means
to do me or my family harm...

743
01:28:11.938 --> 01:28:15.499
<i>then I will do
whatever I can to stop him...</i>

744
01:28:15.608 --> 01:28:18.202
but beyond that...

745
01:28:18.311 --> 01:28:20.211
it's a crapshoot.

746
01:28:24.284 --> 01:28:26.411
The key.

747
01:28:26.519 --> 01:28:29.852
You knew I had jurisdiction...

748
01:28:29.956 --> 01:28:33.722
and would walk you
right out through the front door.

749
01:28:33.827 --> 01:28:35.761
I wanna be left alone.

750
01:28:37.497 --> 01:28:40.125
- Just like that?
- Yeah. Just like that.

751
01:28:45.805 --> 01:28:47.636
This is the man
you've been looking for.

752
01:28:50.376 --> 01:28:53.937
Ballistics will confirm
he was shot by your weapon.

753
01:28:54.047 --> 01:28:56.447
The magazine is in the nightstand
next to your bed.

754
01:28:56.549 --> 01:28:58.779
Don't forget it when
you call your superiors.

755
01:28:58.885 --> 01:29:00.876
Did you kill him here?

756
01:29:00.987 --> 01:29:04.184
It's 5:00. If you wait a few hours,
until the girls go to school...

757
01:29:04.290 --> 01:29:06.190
you won't have to
expose them to this.

758
01:29:06.292 --> 01:29:08.590
Explains why you waited so long
before you called it in.

759
01:29:08.695 --> 01:29:11.664
- I can't go along with this.
- I hope you can.

760
01:29:13.566 --> 01:29:15.830
For both our sakes.

761
01:29:17.237 --> 01:29:19.205
Good-bye, Michael.

762
01:29:24.777 --> 01:29:26.745
I hope I never see you again.

763
01:30:01.114 --> 01:30:04.515
I told you to leave her alone.
You should have listened.

764
01:30:05.515 --> 01:30:15.515
Downloaded From www.AllSubs.org
